 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad 17.2 or newer to be in the path. It can be found in the
 WHDLoad package.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 1.0 MB OtherMem.
 It can be quit by pressing num '*' (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate requester.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.

 Install from the original GrandPrixCircuit disk. The installer copies the
 game files into a data subdirectory. You can also select disk images; the
 installer explains which additional tools are needed.


 Features:
 ---------
 Original installation by JOTD: disk protection removed, support for fast
 memory and 68020+ CPUs, music fixes, manual, icon and source code included.

 Enhanced framerate (CUSTOM2=1) is enabled by the game icon. It provides
 smoother movement on 68020+ CPUs, smoother road, opponent and horizon
 rendering, and more precise roadside and opponent-car positioning on
 68020+ CPUs.

 Set CUSTOM2=0 to use the original simulation and rendering. The screen,
 horizon, Monza and music fixes remain active. The new enhancements and
 game fixes support the original v1 game executable.


 History:
 --------
 version 2.0b (13.10.26):
 - added Enhanced framerate option (CUSTOM2=1), enabled by the game icon
 - smoother vehicle movement on 68020 and faster CPUs
 - smoother road-camera, opponent-car and horizon movement
 - more precise roadside and opponent-car positioning on 68020 and faster CPUs
 - improved drawing performance
 - fixed screen flicker and missing pixels at the edge of the horizon
 - fixed incorrect grid positions and disappearing opponents at Monza
 - fixed missing and cut-off music notes on fast CPUs
 - requires WHDLoad 17.2 or newer


 Contact:
 --------
 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, EXPCHIP, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page or create a mantis issue directly
 at http://mantis.whdload.de

